est and found that their sample mean weight is $144g$ and the sample standard deviation is $s = 20g$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The critical region for the test statistic is approximately $T \\le 1.998$\n2. At the $5%$ level of significance, there is **insufficient** evidence that $μ > 140g$\n3. At the $5%$ level of significance, there is **sufficient** evidence that $μ > 140g$\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $T$ that has a student's $t$-distribution $T_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom, the table below shows the $t$-scores $t_{k, p}$ such that $P(T > t_{k, p}) = p$ for some particular values of $k$ and $p$.*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $23$ | $1.319$ | $1.714$ | $2.069$ | $2.500$ | $2.807$ |\n| $24$ | $1.318$ | $1.711$ | $2.064$ | $2.492$ | $2.797$ |\n| $25$ | $1.316$ | $1.708$ | $2.060$ | $2.485$ | $2.787$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172355 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168994} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168995} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168996} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168997} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168998}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168993}] :question/math-academy-id "q-159361" :question/problem "A fertilizer manufacturer claims that the weight of potatoes produced using their fertilizer has population mean $μ = 9oz$. A farmer who uses their product samples $100$ potatoes from their field and finds th